---
description: A new helper has one short test; a moved method keeps its old test
globs: packages/engine/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Engine tests

A new function gets a short test beside it. The test builds its own bytes and uses an invented label.

A method that stays on the prototype stays covered by the test that already calls it (`Object.create(PlayGame.prototype)`, or `ScenePlayer.prototype.stayJack`). That scenario is not copied into a second file.

Splitting a test file keeps every assertion. Cut on an existing `describe`. When two files need the same setup, it lives in `play/testing.ts`.

```ts
// Wrong: a second stayJack test after the body moved to scene/player-jack.ts.
expect(player.stayJack()).toBe(true);

// Right: the old test still calls the prototype, and pad2 has its own short test.
expect(pad2(3)).toBe("03");
```
